#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:88
msgid ""
"|morpheus| automatically seeds MySQL, Redis and RabbitMQ PCF Instance Types,"
" as well as a generic Cloud Foundry Instance Type that will create a shell "
"app used in conjunction with deployments. PCF Marketplace items can also be "
"added to the Provisioning Library in the Cloud detail view Marketplace tab. "
"The Marketplace item will be added to the selected Instance Type and "
"available when selecting the Cloud Foundry Cloud during Instance or App "
"Template creation."
msgstr ""
"|morpheus| automáticamente seeds MySQL, Redis y RabbitMQ PCF Instance Types,"
" así como un generic Cloud Foundry Instance Type que será create un shell "
"app used in conjunction con deployments. PCF Marketplace elementos puede "
"también be agregado to el Provisioning Library in el Cloud vista de detalles"
" Marketplace pestaña. The Marketplace elemento será be agregado to el "
"seleccionado Instance Type y disponible cuando selecting el Cloud Foundry "
"Cloud durante Instance o App Template creation."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:91
msgid "Deployments"
msgstr "Deployments"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:93
msgid ""
"The Cloud Foundry App Instance Type is used in conjunction with deployments."
" Users do not have to pick deployment when creating a Cloud Foundry App "
"Instance Type, but then Instance will only be a shell of a Cloud Foundry "
"Application."
msgstr ""
"The Cloud Foundry App Instance Type es used in conjunction con deployments. "
"Users no tienen to pick deployment cuando creating un Cloud Foundry App "
"Instance Type, pero entonces Instance será solo be un shell of un Cloud "
"Foundry Application."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:95
msgid ""
"A deployment in Morpheus can either point to a git hub repository or contain"
" the actual manifest.yml and associated artifacts required for a Cloud "
"Foundry deployment.  During the deployment, Morpheus will gather up the "
"files required.  Therefore, if the deployment points to a git hub "
"repository, Morpheus will fetch the files from git hub.  Once the files are "
"obtained, Morpheus will deploy the artifacts in a similar fashion to the "
"Cloud Foundry cli.  This includes parsing the manifest to obtain the "
"parameters to create or update the Cloud Foundry application.  Morpheus will"
" ignore certain fields such as memory and disk size because they are "
"dictated by the selected plan.  Other fields are utilized such as routes.  "
"After parsing the manifest.yml file (including overwriting certain fields), "
"Morpheus is ready to update or create the App in Cloud Foundry."
msgstr ""
"A deployment in Morpheus puede either point to un git hub repository o "
"contain el actual manifest.yml y associated artifacts requerido para un "
"Cloud Foundry deployment.  During el deployment, Morpheus será gather up el "
"archivos requerido.  Por lo tanto, if el deployment points to un git hub "
"repository, Morpheus será fetch el archivos desde git hub.  Once el archivos"
" son obtained, Morpheus será deploy el artifacts in un similar fashion to el"
" Cloud Foundry cli.  This includes parsing el manifest to obtain el "
"parámetros to create o update el Cloud Foundry application.  Morpheus será "
"ignore certain campos como memory y disk tamaño porque they son dictated by "
"el seleccionado plan.  Other campos son utilized como routes.  After parsing"
" el manifest.yml archivo (including overwriting certain campos), Morpheus es"
" ready to update o create el App in Cloud Foundry."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:97
msgid ""
"After the App is configured, the artifacts references in the Morpheus "
"deployment are uploaded to Cloud Foundry for the App.  Note that when paths "
"are referenced in the manifest.yml file, the paths continue to be relative "
"to the manifest.  So, a jar file under build/libs would need to be found "
"under the build/libs directory."
msgstr ""
"After el App es configurado, el artifacts references in el Morpheus "
"deployment son uploaded to Cloud Foundry para el App.  Tenga en cuenta que "
"cuando paths son referenced in el manifest.yml archivo, el paths continue to"
" be relative to el manifest.  So, un jar archivo under build/libs sería need"
" to be found under el build/libs directorio."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:99
msgid ""
"If Cloud Foundry services are specified in the manifest, they must already "
"exist within Cloud Foundry.  Morpheus App templates can be utilized to wire "
"up Cloud Foundry services created by Morpheus.  In this case, Morpheus will "
"add all of the included service names defined in the App template to the "
"manifest.yml services section.  Therefore, multiple services can be used and"
" wired up by Morpheus.”"
msgstr ""
"If Cloud Foundry servicios son especificado in el manifest, they debe ya "
"exist dentro de Cloud Foundry.  Morpheus App templates puede be utilized to "
"wire up Cloud Foundry servicios creado by Morpheus.  In este case, Morpheus "
"será add todos of el incluido servicio names definido in el App template to "
"el manifest.yml servicios sección.  Por lo tanto, múltiples servicios puede "
"be used y wired up by Morpheus.”"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:102
msgid "Example"
msgstr "Ejemplo"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:104
msgid ""
"To better understand how Morpheus parses the manifest.yml file, lets take a "
"closer look at the Cloud Foundry 'spring-music' project.  The project can be"
" found here (https://github.com/cloudfoundry-samples/spring-music)."
msgstr ""
"To better understand how Morpheus parses el manifest.yml archivo, lets take "
"un closer look at el Cloud Foundry 'spring-music' project.  The project se "
"puede encontrar aquí (https://github.com/cloudfoundry-samples/spring-music)."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:106
msgid ""
"The project contains the required manifest.yml file as well as the source "
"code and build.gradle file to define how the project is to be built.  After "
"downloading the project to your local machine, build the project to generate"
" the jar."
msgstr ""
"The project contains el requerido manifest.yml archivo así como el origen "
"code y build.gradle archivo to define how el project es to be built.  After "
"downloading el project to your local machine, build el project to generate "
"el jar."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:108
msgid "Now, let's take a look at the manifest.yml file:"
msgstr "Now, let's take un look at el manifest.yml archivo:"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:110
msgid ""
"---\n"
"applications:\n"
"- name: spring-music\n"
"  memory: 1G\n"
"  random-route: true\n"
"  path: build/libs/spring-music.jar"
msgstr ""
"---\n"
"applications:\n"
"- nombre: spring-music\n"
"  memory: 1G\n"
"  random-route: true\n"
"  ruta: build/libs/spring-music.jar"

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:120
msgid ""
"Using the Cloud Foundry docs (https://docs.cloudfoundry.org/devguide/deploy-"
"apps/manifest.html), we can gain a better understanding of how this file is "
"utilized by Cloud Foundry."
msgstr ""
"Usar Cloud Foundry docs (https://docs.cloudfoundry.org/devguide/deploy-"
"apps/manifest.html), we can gain a better understanding of how this file is "
"utilized by Cloud Foundry."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:122
msgid ""
"The ``-name`` parameter defines the name that will be given to the "
"application in Cloud Foundry.  Morpheus will overwrite this value with the "
"name given to the Instance being created in Morpheus."
msgstr ""
"The ``-name`` parámetro defines el nombre que será be given to el "
"application in Cloud Foundry.  Morpheus será overwrite este valor con el "
"nombre given to el Instance being creado in Morpheus."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:124
msgid ""
"The ``-memory`` parameter (as well as the disk_quota parameter if specified)"
" will be overwritten by Morpheus based on the plan specified for the "
"Instance."
msgstr ""
"The ``-memory`` parámetro (así como el disk_quota parámetro if especificado)"
" será be overwritten by Morpheus basado en el plan especificado para el "
"Instance."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:126
msgid ""
"The ``-path`` parameter defines, where relative to the manifest.yml file, "
"your Cloud Foundry application can be found."
msgstr ""
"The ``-path`` parámetro defines, donde relative to el manifest.yml archivo, "
"your Cloud Foundry application se puede encontrar."

#: ../../integration_guides/Clouds/cloudfoundry/cloudfoundry.rst:128
